      "content": "The problem originates in the `Block._slice` implementation (and the related `Block.take`) in **pandas/core/internals.py** \u2013 it returns a view of the original NumPy array. When that array is read\u2011only the view is also read\u2011only, and later pandas code tries to make it writable, raising the \u201cbuffer source array is read\u2011only\u201d error.\n\nFixing the bug requires changing the slice/take logic to always return a **writable copy** when the source array is read\u2011only. Updating `pandas/core/internals.py` (specifically the `Block._slice` and `Block.take` methods) to copy the data when `self.values.flags.writeable` is `False` resolves the issue and makes `df.iloc[...]` work with read\u2011only DataFrames. \n\n**File to modify**\n- `pandas/core/internals.py`",
